<title>UK: Regan gets extension to court order in CWS battle.</title>
<headline>Regan gets extension to court order in CWS battle.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Andrew Regan, the entrepreneur masterminding a takeover of Britain's Co-operative Wholesale Society (CWS), has been granted an extra 18 hours to prepare an affidavit by a London court, his spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;He has been given an 18-hour extension to submit affidavits,&quot; the spokesman told Reuters, adding Regan had also replied to a letter from CWS chief executive Graham Melmoth. Regan's audacious plan to buy the 153-year-old CWS was thwarted last week when the Co-op obtained an order preventing him from using any confidential information.</p>
</text>
